From f6385d82c2f8aca08012588aad379577c42faed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:58:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(multiaxis): continuous C-axis live tooling - stated
 C on cl moves, the C word in the lathe post

cl::Move gains `rotary` (the spindle's unwrapped C, degrees) beside the
part-frame tip and axis; cl::stamp_c stamps a radially posed path and
splits it until the machine's C-linear motion follows each verified
chord to tolerance. The rotary letter gate admits the spindle's C and the
rotary kinds stamp their paths; check_document reads the stated C. The
stream carries PARAM LiveTool + C; the engine refuses it for scripts
without liveTooling; fanuc-lathe.cps posts X(dia) Z C under G98 with the
machine's own tool_station.live_tool words (new .mch statement), refusing
by name what it cannot voice. Goldens unchanged when no C is stated.

Refs #33

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
